# TimewGUI — Project Intelligence

## Critical Implementation Paths
- All `timew` CLI interactions go through `TimewCli.kt` — never call `timew` directly from UI code
- All CLI methods return `Result<T>` — always handle both `onSuccess` and `onFailure`
- After any mutation (delete, modify, tag, etc.), call `refreshIntervals()` on `TimelineViewModel`
- ViewModels use `CoroutineScope(SupervisorJob() + Dispatchers.Main.immediate)` for UI-safe coroutine launching
- Task CRUD goes through `TaskRepository` → `TaskViewModel` — tasks are persisted to `~/.config/timewgui/tasks.json`
- Tasks link to time intervals via generated tags (`task:<slug>`) from `TaskRepository.generateTag()`

## Theme & Styling
- The theme is "African Savanna" with warm earth tones, NOT the neutral gray/blue from the PRD
- Custom colors are in `TimewColors`, accessed via `LocalTimewColors.current` — do NOT use Material3 `colorScheme` directly for custom tokens
- Tag colors use 8 earth-tone slots defined in `Color.kt` (`TagColorPair` list)
- Times and durations must always use monospace font (`TimewTypography.monospace`)
- Timeline blocks use 0px border radius (sharp corners) — this is intentional for precision aesthetics
- Dashboard banner is a custom Canvas drawing (savanna sunset) — not an image resource
- Dark mode cards use dedicated `textOnCardPrimary/Secondary/Tertiary` tokens — do NOT use regular text colors on card surfaces

## Build & Run
- Always use `make run` or `./gradlew run` to launch (foreground)
- For agent UI verification: `make run-bg` → `make wait-window` → `make screenshot` → read `screenshots/latest.png`
- Or use `make dev-feedback` for the full stop → start → wait → screenshot cycle
- JAVA_HOME must point to OpenJDK 21 (set automatically by Makefile)
- First launch may crash with MetalRedrawer error on macOS — just run again
- Compilation takes ~1.5 min for full rebuild, ~12s for incremental

## Known Gotchas
- `kotlinx.datetime.Instant` is deprecated in favor of `kotlin.time.Instant` — new code should use `kotlin.time.Instant`
- `Icons.Outlined.Label` is deprecated — use `Icons.AutoMirrored.Outlined.Label` instead
- `compose.material3` dependency needs `@Suppress("DEPRECATION")` in build.gradle.kts
- Dark mode `cardSurface` is warm off-white (#FFF5E8) — text on cards must use `textOnCard*` tokens for contrast
- No test infrastructure exists yet — when adding tests, use `src/test/kotlin/`
- App icons (icns/ico) don't exist yet — packaging targets will fail until created (icon.png exists)
- `JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS` env var is NOT visible in process command line — use `-PinstanceId=` Gradle property instead for `pgrep -f` matching
- Python 3.14 on macOS enforces PEP 668 — always use `.dev/venv/` for pip installs, never `--break-system-packages`
- `screencapture` requires Screen Recording permission for the calling app (Cursor) — one-time macOS grant via System Settings
- `LazyColumn` cannot be nested inside `Column(Modifier.verticalScroll())` — use `weight(1f)` for bounded height
- Kotlin property setters can conflict with JVM names (e.g. `setEnabled` vs `isEnabled`) — rename methods to avoid

## User Preferences
- The sidebar branding is "TimeTrackAI" (not "TimewGUI")
- Design language emphasizes warmth and earth tones over clinical precision
- Information density is valued — avoid unnecessary whitespace or decorative elements
- Canvas-based rendering preferred for timeline visualizations (better performance and control)

## File Organization
- Domain logic: `domain/` (model + CLI + repository)
- UI state: `viewmodel/`
- UI rendering: `ui/` (theme, components, screens, navigation)
- Each screen in `ui/screens/` connects components to ViewModels
- Reusable composables in `ui/components/`
- Dev tooling: `scripts/` (dev-screenshot.sh), `.dev/` (runtime state), `screenshots/` (captured images)
- Agent rules: `.cursor/rules/` (dev-feedback-loop.mdc)
- Agent skills: `.cursor/skills/` (update-memory-bank)
- Memory bank: `memory-bank/` (projectbrief, productContext, activeContext, systemPatterns, techContext, progress)
